# Supabase security

- Use publishable keys in the browser; never commit secret or service-role keys.
- Treat `auth.uid()` as the database identity and enforce ownership in RLS.
- Every table in `public` must have RLS enabled before client grants are added.
- `UPDATE` policies require both `USING` and `WITH CHECK`, plus a matching select policy.
- Do not use user-editable metadata for authorization.
- Index foreign keys and recurring RLS/filter columns.
- Make schema changes through a new migration; keep destructive changes explicit and reviewable.
- Run Supabase advisors after applying migrations to a remote project.
